<description>
Before eae193e750235e4023b3e6313284eede2cd7a022, Connect() only started the connection and returned true. If tor wasn't running the refusal was reported later and only logged under -debug=tor. Since eae193e750 (in v32), every failed reconnect attempt logs:

```
2026-11-04T14:14:08Z connect() to 127.0.0.1:9051 failed after wait: Connection refused (111)
2026-11-04T14:14:08Z [warning] tor: Error connecting to address 127.0.0.1:9051
2026-11-04T14:14:08Z [warning] tor: Initiating connection to Tor control port 127.0.0.1:9051 failed
```

On a default configured node without tor, this pollutes debug.log with 18 lines every hour.

This improves it
</description>

<commits>
e998f12b55 torcontrol: Log when an active onion service is lost

11486ab3c8 torcontrol: Warn about failed connections only if Tor control is configured

The Tor control thread retries the connection indefinitely. Previously
every failed attempt logged two warnings plus an info line from netbase,
even for default nodes where the user never asked for Tor.

Only warn if the user explicitly configured Tor control with
-listenonion, -torcontrol or -torpassword, and treat the connection as
manual in that case. Otherwise log failures at debug level only. The
redundant "Initiating connection" warning is removed.

Co-authored-by: Matthew Zipkin <pinheadmz@pm.me>
</commits>

